          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Symmetric spectra are one version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/highly+structured+spectra"} highly structured spectra
            that support a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric monoidal smash product of spectra
            %em symmetric spectrum
            is a sequence of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            which are compatibly equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            %em symmetric spectra
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} symmetric monoidal (∞,1)-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} of spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
            such as to yield itself a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category+of+spectra"} model category of spectra
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+symmetric+spectra"} model structure on symmetric spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+smash+product+of+spectra"} symmetric smash product of spectra
            an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E-%E2%88%9E+ring"} E-∞ ring
            is presented simply as a plain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} in
            symmetric spectra. This is of course such that truncating down to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            yields equivalently the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
            with its usual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product+of+spectra"} smash product of spectra
          %p
            The main technical issue with symmetric spectra is that the naive definition of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            for them is not general homotopy correct, one needs to replace by a “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semistable+symmetric+spectrum"}> semistable symmetric spectrum
            ” first, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#HomotopyGroups"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
            (these however need to be based on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            instead of
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#InComponents In components
          %p
            A symmetric spectrum is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+spectrum"} sequential spectrum
            equipped with an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
            on each component space, such that the structure maps
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intertwiner"} intertwine
            these actions combined with the canonical permutation action on the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
          #SymmetricSpectrum.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong symmetric spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a sequence
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
